[B]About[/B]

Unofficial CyanogenMod 10 (Android 4.1.2 Jelly Bean) port for the LG L5 II E450g, codename [B]vee5ss[/B], SoC MediaTek MT6575.

It runs on the stock prebuilt kernel. The vendor HALs (audio, camera, lights, RIL, video codecs) are loaded through small wrappers in the device tree instead of patching CyanogenMod, and the code shared with the LG L4 II now lives in a common tree, [B]mt6575-common[/B].

[B]Build 3 news:[/B] the zip now flashes the boot image by itself (no more dd), Bluetooth uses LG's stock MediaTek app, video recording and playback use the MediaTek hardware codecs, the home key LED behaves like stock, and the RIL wrapper now accepts incoming calls and attaches mobile data by itself.

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: LG L5 II / LG-E450g
[*]Codename: vee5ss
[*]SoC: MediaTek MT6575, ARMv7-A Cortex-A9, 1 GHz
[*]GPU: PowerVR SGX531
[*]RAM: 512 MB
[*]Display: 4.0" 480×800 hdpi
[*]Storage: 4 GB internal / external microSD
[*]Android: 4.1.2 Jelly Bean (JZO54K)
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working (tested on Build 3):[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Boot, display, touchscreen, PowerVR SGX531 hardware acceleration
[*]WiFi (MT6620)
[*][B]Bluetooth[/B] with LG's stock MediaTek Bluetooth app (MtkBt), as on the stock ROM: pairing, sending and receiving files (OPP). Pairings survive reboots and Bluetooth turns itself back on at boot.
[*]Audio: speaker, earpiece, microphone, wired headset (plug/unplug switches the output)
[*][B]FM radio[/B] with its own app (wired headphones as the antenna): headphones or speaker, seek, scan, favorites, station name (RDS), keeps playing with the screen off
[*]Camera: photos (5 MP) and preview
[*][B]Video recording with the MediaTek hardware encoder[/B]: MPEG-4 640×480 at up to 30 fps with AAC audio
[*][B]Video playback with the MediaTek hardware decoder[/B]: H.264 Baseline, Main and High, MPEG-4 and H.263, up to 1280×720
[*][B]Home key LED like stock[/B]: color pattern while booting, charging pattern with the screen off, green when full, shutdown pattern, notifications
[*]LCD brightness
[*]Sensors: accelerometer, compass, proximity
[*]USB MTP: internal storage and microSD
[*]Internal storage and external microSD
[*]Modem boots, IMEI and baseband shown, SIM detected
[*]zRAM swap (Settings → Performance)
[*]ADB root (development build)
[/LIST]

[B]Not tested on Build 3[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Calls, SMS and mobile data: my test unit is carrier-locked, so I could not check them on this phone. They use the same RIL wrapper as the LG L4 II build, where incoming and outgoing calls, SMS and mobile data are confirmed working (Entel Peru). The radio side (modem, IMEI, SIM) comes up here.
[*]WiFi hotspot and USB tethering
[*]MMS
[*]GPS: the stock GPS daemon is included, not tested yet
[*]Bluetooth audio (A2DP headphones/speakers)
[/LIST]

[B]Known issues[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]1080p video does not play[/B]: the MT6575 video decoder only goes up to 1280×720 (same as stock).
[*][B]No H.264 video recording[/B]: the camera records MPEG-4 instead; CyanogenMod's MP4 writer rejects the MediaTek H.264 encoder output.
[*][B]Carrier-locked phones[/B] show "SIM network unlock PIN" with a SIM from another carrier. The ROM cannot remove a carrier lock; tap Dismiss to keep using the phone.
[*][B]MediaScanner crash[/B]: folders on the microSD with Latin-1 encoded names (for example "Imágenes" written by an old PC) make MediaScanner abort. Rename or remove them from a PC.
[/LIST]

[B]Important notes[/B]
[LIST]
[*]This ROM is for the [B]LG-E450g (vee5ss) only[/B], the only variant I could test. Do not flash it on other L5 II variants.
[*]You need an unlocked bootloader and TWRP: see my [B]How To Root and Unlock the Bootloader LG L5 II E450g[/B] guide and the [B]TWRP 3.1.1-0.2 for LG L5 II E450g[/B] thread.
[*][B]Back up your NVRAM[/B] (IMEI and calibration) before flashing any MTK ROM.
[*]GApps: use a Jelly Bean (4.1) package.
[/LIST]

[B]Requirements[/B]
[LIST]
[*]LG-E450g (vee5ss)
[*]Unlocked bootloader + TWRP 3.1.1-0.2 for LG L5 II
[*]At least 30% battery
[*]Full Nandroid backup
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Download:[/B][/SIZE]

[URL="PUT_DOWNLOAD_LINK_HERE"]cm-10-20261026-UNOFFICIAL-vee5ss.zip[/URL]

[CODE]MD5: c4b40070708dd94e9057102d17ff496a[/CODE]

[B]Install: clean flash (recommended)[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Copy the zip to your microSD.
[*]Boot into TWRP and make a full backup.
[*]Wipe: Data, Cache, Dalvik Cache (your internal storage is kept).
[*]Install the zip. It writes /system and the boot image.
[*]Optional: install a Jelly Bean GApps package.
[*]Reboot System. The first boot takes a few minutes.
[/LIST]

[B]Install: update from Build 2[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Boot into TWRP and make a backup.
[*]Install the new zip (no separate boot.img any more).
[*]Wipe Cache and Dalvik Cache.
[*]Reboot System.
[/LIST]

[B]Troubleshooting[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]A Bluetooth device you paired before updating cannot connect[/B]: forget the pairing on both phones and pair again from the L5 II.
[*][B]Bootloop after flashing[/B]: wipe Cache and Dalvik Cache in TWRP and reboot.
[*][B]A video says "Can't play this video"[/B]: check its resolution; anything above 1280×720 is not supported by the hardware.
[/LIST]

