[B]Changelog[/B]

[B]2026-10-25 — Build 3[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]The zip flashes the boot image itself[/B], in MediaTek format. No more dd from the TWRP shell.
[*][B]Bluetooth[/B]: LG's stock MediaTek Bluetooth app replaces CyanogenMod's, as on the stock ROM (CyanogenMod's app froze trying to open sockets this stack does not provide). Fixed pairings being lost (the stack's device database could not be written), the receive dialog crash, and Bluetooth staying off after a reboot.
[*][B]Video recording[/B]: MediaTek hardware encoder, MPEG-4 640×480 with AAC (was 320×240 software encoding). Fixed green/magenta colors in recorded videos.
[*][B]Video playback[/B]: MediaTek hardware decoder for H.264 Main/High and MPEG-4 up to 720p (CyanogenMod's software decoder only played H.264 Baseline). Fixed H.264 videos stuttering or standing still: the MediaTek decoder drops the frame timestamps, the codec wrapper now restores them; 720p plays smoothly.
[*][B]FM radio[/B]: new app with the look of Android's own FM Radio, on LG's stock FM libraries and audio HAL.
[*]adb, CyanogenMod and the updated TWRP report the phone's own serial, the same as the stock ROM, instead of 0123456789ABCDEF.
[*]Dalvik heap as on the stock ROM (64 MB per app), so heavier apps have more room.
[*]The zip writes the boot image safely: rebooting with the power key right after flashing could leave a phone that does not boot.
[*][B]Home key LED[/B]: same behavior as LG's stock service (boot pattern, charging/full patterns with the screen off, shutdown pattern); fixed the boot color pattern never stopping.
[*][B]Telephony[/B]: the RIL wrapper now does the MediaTek work of the stock framework: it accepts incoming calls (before, they never rang), attaches to GPRS when the radio turns on, adds the data call parameter mtk-ril needs, and reports call progress so the call screen follows the call. Confirmed on the L4 II, which shares it.
[*]APNs for Claro, Movistar and Entel Peru; SIM Toolkit added.
[*]Audio, camera, lights and RIL now use device-tree wrappers around the stock HALs instead of CyanogenMod patches. Fixed a crash when recording video.
[*]Shared code with the LG L4 II moved to the new mt6575-common tree.
[/LIST]

[B]2026-06-30 — Build 2[/B]
[LIST]
[*]IMEI fix: stock lgpserver reads it from /dev/misc2.
[*]RIL waits for the modem channels before starting; baseband version and IMEI retried on radio on.
[*]zRAM enabled (ro.zram.default=25).
[*]Modem boots on the first attempt.
[*]SIM PIN prompt shown on boot.
[*]WiFi, Bluetooth and outgoing calls confirmed.
[/LIST]

[B]2026-06-22 — Build 1 (initial public test)[/B]
[LIST]
[*]First bootable CM10 build for LG-E450g / vee5ss: MediaTek boot image, PowerVR SGX531 blobs, MTK radio stack, custom lights HAL, sensors, microSD.
[/LIST]

